          "path": "_m/g/f/5/v/boreraig-wp/boreraig-geograph-org-uk-15398.jpg",
          "filename": "Boreraig - geograph.org.uk - 1539814.jpg",
          "caption": "Boreraig Boreraig is one of the best, most intact, examples of a cleared village on Skye. It lies on the north shore of Loch Eishort and is reached either by boat or by a walk of some four miles across the moor from Strath Suardal. On the right can be seen a natural hollow in the standing stone, in which visitors have left coins.",
